            "be1261240045_html": "Can I decant it or use it in foggers, humidifiers or HVAC?",
            "be241535854_html": " What if small amounts contact food or are incidentally ingested?",
            "be1635367347_html": "Which SanOT product should I choose?",
            "be800679950_html": "Are there any disclaimers or precautions when considering SanOT products",
            "be1942287050_html": "Hypochlorous acid (HOCl) is the same antimicrobial your white blood cells produce. SanOT\u2019s water-based formulations reduce microbial load quickly when used as directed\u2014without the flammability\/dehydration of alcohols or the harshness often associated with bleach or certain quats. Clean, comfortable finish for frequent use.",
            "be2010811025_html": "Proven effective against a broad scope of bacteria, fungi, spores, and viruses when used as directed (see each product\u2019s intended use).",
            "be1343742131_html": "Use on the areas listed for each product (skin\/eyes\/food\/gear\/animals\/plants\/surfaces). You may apply frequently\u2014even back-to-back. Maintain ~60\u201390 seconds contact time (keep the area visibly wet) or allow to air-dry, unless the page states otherwise.",
            "be1430268432_html": "If soiled, clean first (water; or appropriate detergent for heavier soiling), then apply. Most uses are no-rinse; for food or mouth-contact items, you may wipe\/rinse if you prefer.",
            "be466096780_html": "Yes. All SanOT HOCl is produced to food- and medical-grade standards for antimicrobial efficacy. Where helpful for the audience, some pages also show Halaal and HACCP-suitable badges.",
            "be1877767551_html": "A light, clean sea-water \/ ozone-like note that dissipates quickly.",
            "be571818532_html": "HOCl acts via multiple oxidative mechanisms (proteins, lipids, DNA\/RNA), so resistance development is considered unlikely. Always use as directed.",
            "be903453334_html": "Yes\u2014into clean, compatible containers\/devices only. For ULV\/fogging\/HVAC, follow facility SOPs. Do not heat or mix with additives.",
            "be240657394_html": "Food-grade formulas are intended for directed food uses; they are not beverages. Incidental residue from food applications is expected; for large accidental ingestion, drink water.",
            "be1973010887664_html": "<ul><li><b>Skin\/eyes (human):<\/b> San-Ocular, San-O-Wound, San-O-Eczema, MOON Aftersun, San-O-Sport (skin).\n<\/li><li><b>Baby:<\/b> San-O-Baby Topical (skin), San-O-Baby Accessories &amp; Toys (objects).\n<\/li><li><b>Intimate:<\/b> San-O-Intimate (external, intravaginal, toy hygiene).\n<\/li><li><b>Surfaces\/air: <\/b>San-O-Tizer (general), San-O-Doc (clinical).\n<\/li><li><b>Food:<\/b> San-O-Fresh.\n<\/li><li><b>Veterinary\/animals:<\/b> San-O-Vet (general), San-O-Vet Eyecare (ocular).\n<\/li><li><b>Agri:<\/b> San-O-Agri Light (home\/nursery), San-O-Agri Extra (high-load\/agri &amp; packhouse).<\/li><\/ul><div>\n<\/div><div>\n<\/div><div>\n<\/div><div>\n<\/div><div>\n<\/div><div>\n<\/div>",
            "be1025157177_html": "Avoid direct eye contact unless the product specifically indicates ocular use; wipe\/rinse metals after use (not typically required for 316 stainless steel); avoid sensitive fabrics; if sensitivity occurs, rinse with cool water and discontinue; do not mix with other chemicals\/products; if ingested flush with plenty of clean water.",
            "be1840590792_html": "San-O-Agri Extra",
            "be1508067001_html": "Where and how should I use it (vs Light)?",
            "be1982419371_html": "What systems\/materials is it suitable for?",
            "be398375912_html": "A higher-strength option for high-load zones (greenhouses, packhouses, wash lines). Dilute to suit foliar sprays, tools\/equipment sanitation, post-harvest rinses and room\/line turnover per your SOPs.",
            "be703613670_html": "Structures, walkways, tools\/trays, harvest totes, wash lines, packaging benches, cold-room seals, transport crates and irrigation\/hydro hardware\u2014compatible with sprayers, misters, foggers and wash lines. Does not adversely affect pollinators when used as directed.",
            "be1834585794_html": "San-O-Agri Light",
            "be64430939_html": "What plants\/environments and tasks is it for?",
            "be2026868019_html": "Is it a pesticide? Will it affect pollinators?",
            "be1007581162_html": "For homes and nurseries\u2014indoor, greenhouse and garden plants. Use for microbial hygiene on leaves\/canopies, benches, trays, tools, propagation\/cuttings, seed\/seedling prep and plant wound sites.",
            "be924137120_html": "Not a pesticide; it targets microbial hygiene. It may disrupt pest life cycles indirectly by improving surface hygiene, but it\u2019s not intended for insects. Does not adversely affect pollinators when used as directed.",
            "be779503815_html": "San-O-Baby Accessories &amp; Toys",
            "be691229650_html": "Which items\/materials and do I need to rinse?",
            "be676668280_html": "Is it safe for everyday nursery use?",
            "be203986039_html": "Can I use it on wood, fabric or electronics?",
            "be1612917366_html": "What\u2019s the difference between this and San-O-Baby Topical Spray?",
            "be1005985571_html": "Use on hard, non-porous baby items: pacifiers, nipples, bottles, utensils, teethers, toys, play mats, changing tables, high chairs, lunch boxes, stroller trays, etc. Mist to wet; allow contact time; air-dry. For mouth-contact items, you may wipe or rinse if preferred.",
            "be1383097656_html": "Yes\u2014food- and medical-grade; targets common nursery\/clinic pathogens; leaves no residue when used as directed.",
            "be671941023_html": "Wood: light mist and wipe\u2014don\u2019t saturate. Fabrics: spot-test; avoid soaking. Electronics: spray a cloth and wipe housings (avoid ports).",
            "be2142777448_html": "Accessories &amp; Toys is for objects\/surfaces; Topical Spray is for skin.",
            "be110016564_html": "San-O-Baby Topical Spray&nbsp;",
            "be539148422_html": " From what age and for which routines?",
            "be129312174_html": "Can I follow with barrier creams or use soaked gauze?",
            "be923297398_html": "How often can I use it?",
            "be1173408780_html": "From infancy for nappy care, folds, scrapes, bites and minor irritations. Medical-grade antiseptic; anti-inflammatory; won\u2019t strip natural oils.",
            "be1133848933_html": "Yes\u2014apply first, allow contact time, then layer your barrier cream\/gel. For comfort, you can briefly apply gauze\/tissue soaked with product and discard after use.",
            "be663455923_html": "As often as needed.",
            "be1297256675_html": "What can I disinfect\u2014devices, PPE, rooms?",
            "be65686809_html": "How does it slot into workflows?",
            "be33227300_html": "Use on clinical surfaces, non-critical devices, probes, prosthetics, beds and PPE (masks, gloves, shields) per SOPs; suitable for light room-misting where appropriate.",
            "be141749956_html": "Pre-clean visible soil, then disinfect with ~60\u201390 s contact time. Supports fast turnover and end-of-day cleaning; follow device IFUs.",
            "be18124860_html": "Can I combine with prescribed treatments or emollients? Will it dry my skin?",
            "be1939100212_html": "How often and any comfort tips?",
            "be301016293_html": "Yes\u2014apply San-O-Eczema first, allow contact time, then layer your prescribed cream\/gel or emollient. It\u2019s anti-inflammatory and won\u2019t strip natural oils.",
            "be1334927033_html": "Use multiple times daily. For comfort, briefly apply soaked gauze to the area, then discard.",
            "be861557724_html": "Athlete\u2019s foot and odour\u2014how should I use it and on what?",
            "be214523408_html": "Spray soles, heels, between toes and around nail edges; allow contact time; air-dry. For odour control, lightly mist shoes and socks to address odour-causing bacteria.",
            "be2022433858_html": "As frequently as needed.",
            "be528439649_html": "What foods and settings is it for? Do I need to rinse?",
            "be1636055499_html": "Can it help with shelf life and mould?",
            "be2127430812_html": "Compliance?",
            "be1102095239_html": "Use at home or in restaurants on freshly picked produce, store-bought groceries, meats, poultry and seafood. Also for utensils and prep surfaces. Mist to wet; allow contact time; no rinsing required (rinse optional).",
            "be1549382233_html": "Yes\u2014spray before storing foods to help support shelf life in and out of the fridge. You can also spray over visible mould on treated areas to help prevent spread.",
            "be534330887_html": "Food- and medical-grade; Halaal; suitable for HACCP environments.",
            "be889775032_html": "External, intravaginal and toy use\u2014pH, odour, residue?",
            "be1038963570_html": "What is it tested against? Does it prevent STIs or act as contraception?",
            "be1681348182_html": "Toy material notes",
            "be1844414345_html": "Formulated for topical and intravaginal care and hygienic toy surfaces. pH-considerate, neutralises odour-causing bacteria, dries without residue.",
            "be1192479240_html": "Lab-tested effective against Herpes virus and Candida albicans, among others. It is not a contraceptive and does not prevent STIs.",
            "be799926627_html": "Best on non-porous materials (silicone, ABS, stainless steel). For porous\/painted items or electronics, follow manufacturer guidance (spray cloth, not ports).",
            "be1635521718_html": "Can I spray it into my eyes? What about contact lenses?",
            "be998395931_html": "What symptoms can it help with?",
            "be1191057860_html": "Yes\u2014hold ~10 cm away and spray into\/onto eyes and lids; blink to distribute. Use before inserting or after removing contact lenses; don\u2019t spray onto lenses while worn.",
            "be243501291_html": "Useful for dryness\/irritation and hygiene around pink-eye\/stye-related symptoms; suitable for regular daily routines.",
            "be1025604457_html": "What\u2019s it for\u2014skin or equipment?",
            "be1201313511_html": "How do I use it\u2014and can it be a cooling mist?",
            "be1076402309_html": " Will it leave stickiness or odour?",
            "be850880063_html": "Both. Topically for scratches, chafing, rashes, minor scrapes\/blisters and post-workout irritation; and for equipment\/gear from yoga mats and benches to helmets, gloves, mouth guards, weights, bars and pads.",
            "be1089146400_html": "Skin: spray, maintain contact time, air-dry; may be used as a light cooling mist on intact skin. Gear: spray non-porous surfaces, allow contact time, then wipe or dry.",
            "be305936763_html": "No sticky residues; helps deodorise shoes, pads and bags.",
            "be156294190_html": "When do I use it\u2014pre, during or after?",
            "be354904521_html": "Can I soak jewellery in it?",
            "be2062960275_html": "How often may I apply\u2014and can I layer balms?",
            "be1788804399_html": "Will it fade tattoo ink or alter colours?",
            "be183077035_html": "All three: pre-procedure prep, in-process hygiene and post-procedure aftercare (as advised by your professional).",
            "be1273179706_html": "Do not soak jewellery. You may disinfect and wipe jewellery surfaces (or saturate a sterile swab\/gauze) per studio guidance.",
            "be1156704240_html": "You may reapply multiple times in succession before using your prescribed cream\/gel; frequent application generally improves comfort and hygiene.",
            "be592037918_html": "No\u2014won\u2019t bleach or lift colour when used as directed.",
            "be731439200_html": "What does it cover\u2014hands, surfaces, air?",
            "be874795420_html": "How is it different from alcohol sanitisers?",
